        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Glen%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Spring Glen was first settled by a handful of bachelor farmers, starting with James Gay in 1878.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://alchetron.com/Spring-Glen%2C-Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community of Spring Glen became more diverse after 1890 as coal mining brought immigrants from Southern Europe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Glen%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers in Spring Glen were known as nonconformists who were less religious and social than other Utah pioneers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Glen%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A canal company chose the name Spring Glen for both the irrigation project and the village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
